Great roguelike RPG. Once you get to know the mechanics of the game you start to enjoy more of the game and you start to make some awesome plays. The game makes you farm for better armor, weapons, loot, relics and also makes you think before making any movement. At the end of quests you have to recover your heroes from the psychological impacts that the dungeons have caused on them such as stress and/or diseases. Certain strategies are necessary and you also must learn when to retreat (
). Anyways, if you're into RPG's you'll love this game!
Edit: Yes, there's a lot of RNG in this game and sometimes it can be unfair. BUT, the way people complain about this game being hard mostly because of the RNG is unfair. Like I said, you have to prepare for each type of dungeon, select specific character classes, specific relics, administer your resources and above all you have to think before making any move such as engaging in a battle. If your party gets wiped thats awful but the game gives you 20+ characters of 10+ classes to play! If you still find it difficult, farm for better equipment/loot otherwise it will be obviously hard or even impossible. What fun is a game that you can beat in a few hours in?

